{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"864","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Make a Permutation!"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Ivan has an array consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" elements. Each of the elements is an integer from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Recently Ivan learned about permutations and their lexicographical order. Now he wants to change (replace) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"minimum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number of elements in his array in such a way that his array becomes a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"permutation"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" (i.e. each of the integers from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" was encountered in his array exactly once). If there are multiple ways to do it he wants to find the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lexicographically minimal"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation among them."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus minimizing the number of changes has the first priority, lexicographical minimizing has the second priority."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In order to determine which of the two permutations is lexicographically smaller, we compare their first elements. If they are equal — compare the second, and so on. If we have two permutations "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":", then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" is lexicographically smaller if "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xi < yi"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"i"},{"kind":"text","text":" is the first index in which the permutations "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":" differ."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Determine the array Ivan will obtain after performing all the changes."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 200 000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of elements in Ivan's array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains a sequence of integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., an"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the description of Ivan's array."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the minimum number of elements that need to be changed in Ivan's array in order to make his array a permutation. In the second line, print the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lexicographically minimal"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" permutation which can be obtained from array with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"q"},{"kind":"text","text":" changes."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4\n3 2 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n1 2 4 3 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"6\n4 5 6 3 2 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n4 5 6 3 2 1 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n6 8 4 6 7 1 6 3 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n2 8 4 6 7 1 9 3 10 5 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example Ivan needs to replace number three in position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" with number one, and number two in position "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" with number four. Then he will get a permutation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"[1, 2, 4, 3]"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" with only two changed numbers — this permutation is lexicographically minimal among all suitable. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example Ivan does not need to change anything because his array already is a permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"864D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/864/problem/D"}